# Accepted vulnerabilities — suppressed from FAILING the security scan, but still reported as a build WARNING.
# Format: one CVE ID per line; "#" starts a comment; an inline "# reason" is shown in the warning.
# Re-check on every base-image rebuild and remove the entry once the CVE is no longer reported.

# Added 2026-11-05. Ubuntu fixed this in apt 2.8.4ubuntu0.1, but the pinned base (eclipse-temurin:26-jre-noble, see
# dockerBaseImageParam in gradle.properties) still ships apt 2.8.3 as of 2026-11-12; 25-jre-noble rebuilt on 2026-11-11.
# Not exploitable here: the attack needs apt to fetch packages, and the service never runs apt — the image's
# entrypoint is the JVM and nothing installs packages at runtime.
CVE-2026-109518 # apt on-path attack during package fetch; the service never runs apt. Drop when 26-jre-noble rebuilds.

# Previously accepted: CVE-2026-84782 removed 2026-10-03, and CVE-2026-45447 on 2026-07-02, both after the noble
# base rebuilt with patched openssl
